            <ArticleTitle>Advances in LDL-apheresis for the treatment of severe hypercholesterolemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>LDL-apheresis is an extracorporeal plasma-perfusion method that selectively removes apolipoprotein B-containing lipoproteins from the blood. It is indicated for patients with homozygous and drug-resistant heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia. Clinical and angiographic regression of coronary artery disease has been demonstrated in patients treated with cholesterol-lowering programs that include LDL-apheresis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
